@node 01 "Whats This ?..."

  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================

  WarKick'Em is a tool that will allow selected users to kick users from
  other nodes, that is naturally a VERY powerful weapon to put into a
  users hand, an so some kind of security is needed, suffice to say that
  the door asks the user of a reason why is about to kick another user,
  and logs the data the user writes in the callerslog together with a
  datestamp, handle of user about to be kicked and the node # of the user
  about to be kicked. Also, if the user being kicked is idle then the door
  will post a warning to him saying that he will be kicked of in 30 secs.,
  which will aloow the user to log out normally.

  *** Danger *** If the users being kicked is using a door that has a
  poorly written emergency exit code, then it is possible that his node
  will be locked up until the next reboot of the board.

  So why should you install this door, well, just imagine this, some lame
  14.4K user is bugging down your nice and shiny V.34 line, and one of
  super ELI7E trader have just gotten hands on an 1 hour release, wouldn't
  it be nice if the super ELI7E trader could kick the lamer so we would
  be able to get hold of the V.34 line ???

  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================

@endnode

@node 02 "Installation..."

  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================

  Installing this program is really quite simple, the only things you have
  to is to make sure the following is right :

  Program      Location                      Description
  -------      --------                      -----------
  WarKick'Em   Doors:!!!War!!!/WarKick'Em/   Main Program.
  SecList      Doors:!!!War!!!/WarKick'Em/   List Of Users Allowed To Use
                                             The Door Seperated By Cr's.

  Also make sure that kick.info is in the 'Commands/BBSCmd/' drawer.

  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================

@endnode

